## Summary

On a live-session miss, `ds4-server` saves the outgoing session to disk (`reason=evict`) **before** it searches the disk cache for the incoming prompt. When the budget is full, that save runs the eviction pass, and the pass can delete the very prefix entry the lookup on the next line would have loaded. The request then cold-prefills.

With the density bias described in #444, this happens every time rather than by chance. The prefix a divergent request needs is always shorter than the outgoing session snapshot (that snapshot is the prompt plus the generated tokens), so the prefix has the lower `tokens / file_size` and is the first victim.

The workload that hits this is long-document Q&A: one large document, a different question appended each time, one slot. The cold checkpoint of the document is written correctly on every request, but deleted again on the next request before it can be read. It is never loaded.

## Environment

- Code path is identical in upstream `main` @ ee7e840 and @ 5379c1c (`ds4_server.c` around L13609; `ds4_kvstore.c` unchanged). Measured on kernelpool/ds4 `ds41-perf` (based on 5379c1c, no changes to this path).
- macOS, M3 Ultra 256 GB. DeepSeek V4.1 Flash-1017 IQ2_XXS-Q2_K, one slot.
- `--ctx 524288 --kv-disk-space-mb 32768 --kv-cache-cold-max-tokens 600000`. Other disk KV options are defaults.

## Reproduction

The prompts all share a 379K-token document and differ only in the question at the end (≈379,300 tokens each; `common=379235`). They are sent one after another as single user messages, with thinking on. The cache already holds about 13 earlier 380K session files, so it is near the 32 GiB budget.

Request N is cold-prefilled (~11 min) and stores the document prefix:

```
23:21:46 kv cache stored tokens=378880 trimmed=436 reason=cold key=token-text size=2325.56 MiB
```

Request N+1 arrives. The live session misses, as it should, but the evict save deletes that cold entry first:

```
23:23:47 kv cache evicted reason=disk-cache-full tokens=378880 hits=0 size=2325.56 MiB file=…/a1ff87bb….kv
23:23:47 live kv cache miss live=383131 prompt=379300 common=379235 vision=match reason=token-mismatch
23:23:48 kv cache stored tokens=383131 trimmed=0 reason=evict key=thinking-visible size=2351.53 MiB
```

The disk lookup then finds nothing (`cached=0`, 824 s), the request re-stores the same cold file, and the next request deletes it again (`23:36:21 stored … reason=cold`, then `23:37:31 evicted … tokens=378880 … a1ff87bb….kv`).

This repeated for three consecutive requests (cold stores at 23:21, 23:36 and 23:49, each evicted with `hits=0` by the next request's evict save). Note that the evicted prefix was not superseded by anything: the session snapshot that replaced it is useless for every later request, because its key text runs past the divergence point.

The same thing happened later with a 127K-token document after the cache had filled up again. The 124,928-token cold entry was evicted at the next request's evict save, while older zero-hit 380K session files survived.

**With room in the budget the mechanism works:** after raising the budget to 48 GiB, the next 7 requests loaded the prefix (`kv cache hit text tokens=378880 … load=306-1306 ms`, `cached=378880`). They took 76-538 s each, against 824-1087 s for cold prefill.

## Cause

```c
if (!multimodal && s->kv.enabled && cached == 0 &&
    old_pos >= s->kv.opt.min_tokens) {
    kv_cache_store_current(s, slot, "evict");   // may run ds4_kvstore_evict()
}
if (!multimodal && cached == 0) {
    disk_cached = kv_cache_try_load(s, slot, &j->req, &effective_prompt, …);
```

The order itself is deliberate: the live session has to be persisted before a disk load replaces it. But nothing stops that persist step from evicting the load target.

## Proposed fix

Before the evict save, find the entry `ds4_kvstore_try_load_text()` would pick, using `ds4_kvstore_find_text_prefix()` with the same model, quant and ctx filters. Keep it out of the eviction pass for the duration of the save. If only the protected entry is left, the pass stops instead of deleting it.

The change is small and touches only this path:

- a `protect_sha[41]` field in `ds4_kvstore`;
- a skip in `ds4_kvstore_evict()`;
- one server helper, `kv_cache_store_evict_keeping_prefix()`;
- a unit test, `test_kv_cache_eviction_keeps_protected_entry`. It fails 3 times without the `ds4_kvstore.c` change and passes with it. The whole `ds4_test --server` group passes.

The patch applies cleanly to `main` @ ee7e840, and I'm happy to open it as a PR.

This fixes only the ordering hazard. The density bias (#444 / #711) and the continued-checkpoint supersede policy (#1186) are separate. They make this bug deterministic, but they don't cause it.

